course: dictionary
lesson: 4218
title: Graceful things and graceful manners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Graceful describes something that moves or looks smooth, light and beautiful. Think of a dancer turning on one foot, or a swan gliding across a lake.
explain: Context shows you which meaning to use. «Her neck bends in any direction, like a serpent», and she curves it into «a graceful zigzag». A zigzag is a sharp, angular shape, so graceful here means the curves flow smoothly and look elegant, not clumsy. Swap in your meaning and check: a smooth, elegant zigzag still makes sense.
explain: Graceful can also describe good manners. A «graceful loser» shakes hands, says well done and stays kind, even when losing is hard. The clue is the word loser: losing is difficult, so graceful means polite and fair in a tricky moment.
fact: Graceful means moving in a smooth, light and beautiful way.
fact: Graceful can also mean having a beautiful, elegant shape, such as a building.
fact: Graceful can mean polite and kind when things are difficult, as in «a graceful loser».
fact: Serpent is an old word for snake.
fact: Graceful is an adjective: graceful, more graceful, most graceful.
exercise: In «Her neck bends in any direction, like a serpent», what is a serpent? | A tall tree | A bird that swims | *A snake | A kind of dance
exercise: Which sentence uses graceful to mean polite and kind when things are hard? | The old tower had a graceful, elegant shape | The dancer made a graceful spin on one foot | *She was a graceful loser and shook hands with the winner | The swan glided gracefully across the lake
exercise: A swan moves gracefully on the river. What does graceful most likely mean here? | Clumsy and noisy | *Moving in a smooth, light and beautiful way | Cold and wet | Very hungry
test: A winner who praises the other team and stays kind is behaving with what? | Noise | Rudeness | Hunger | *Grace
test: What does a graceful building look like? | Wet and grey | *Elegant, with a beautiful shape | Very loud | Ugly and broken
exam: Her neck curves into «a graceful zigzag». Which word is closest in meaning to graceful here? | Sudden | *Elegant | Messy | Clumsy
